// 'Veach, Ajar' — Benedikt Bitterli (CC0, public domain; crediting the
// artist encouraged). The door-ajar room: the sun enters only through a
// barely-open door, so nearly everything is lit indirectly — the
// difficult-light-transport standard, and this corpus's candidate to
// take brass-room's reuse-gate role at the swap rung
// (docs/corpus-plan.md, decision 6). Official pbrt-v4 export from
// https://benedikt-bitterli.me/resources/ — `scenes/corpus/fetch.sh
// veach-ajar` materializes the source (its TGA textures decode via the
// extension-hinted path texture.rs grew for this scene); this RON was
// bootstrapped once by `cenote-cli import
// sources/bitterli/veach-ajar/scene-v4.pbrt` and is the source of truth
// — re-imports diff into scratch, never over it.
//
// Import fidelity: exact in effect — the importer averages pbrt's u/v
// roughness axes (×4), but every pair here is equal-axis, so the average
// is the identity; the source's per-texture "filter" hints (trilinear,
// ×3) are ignored in favor of cenote's own sampler filtering, cosmetic
// only. This scene's landscape painting is the reason imported UVs (and
// PLY UVs everywhere) land v-flipped: pbrt inverts t at every image
// lookup, and an upside-down lake is how that convention gap announced
// itself.
